PianoThermal is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE). No source file was copied from anywhere. What it takes
from other work, and from where:

Adreno830 (github.com/Shad0w23333/Adreno830, main 1a1321056ffc5428ae925f4680093718b46ca7c2, unixnu.lock pin."Adreno830"), MIT;
in this repository unchanged as package/PianoA830/adreno830/platform/sm8750/Sm8750Tsens.h (sha256
31bfb95b347466bfe01151f7bba3b94159e974062ff09509f75dd60f59f26a79) and Sm8750Tsens.c (sha256
a395406398360589e88e467a1279a4ed490d2f57d477b20c6c8aa818e57c35b0):
  Facts, hardware-verified on the OnePlus 13T (SM8750): TM_Sn_STATUS = TM + 0xa0 + 4n, LAST_TEMP [11:0] signed deci-degrees C,
  VALID bit 21, VALID dropping for a few AHB cycles (retry a few reads). Tsens.h re-implements the decode for all four controllers.

hackios-xnu-kernel, branch k90-port 0e0f19bbba27da57c1845bc16d2415cd38046cab (the REDMI K90 "annibale", SM8750, XNU port; local
unixnu-research/hackios-xnu-kernel-k90), xnu/files/bsd/dev/annibale/annibale_cpufreq.c (sha256
b01bcc372d9293f984f138ad1636553e90181b374af99eb38c6682279b1f17ef), under that repository's APSL-2.0 LICENSE:
  Facts only, no code: on SM8750 the cores' clocks are set by the CPUCP firmware through SCMI's performance protocol 0x13, polled,
  one message at a time in the shared memory at 0x17b4e000 with a doorbell write at 0x17830000 + 0x104; domain 0 = cluster 0
  (six cores), domain 1 = cluster 1 (two); protocol 4.0 with level indexing; "NCC0" 16 levels 384-3532 MHz, "NCC1" 16 levels
  1017-4320 MHz, sustained 4089.6 MHz; the boot loader left domain 1 at its slowest there; the TSENS groups 0x0c228000 sensors
  1-14, 0x0c229000 1-6, 0x0c22a000 1-8 (the port's run: hackios-redmi-k90-annibale docs/progress/2026-10-26-gpu-desktop-acceleration.md). The
  governor's shape (busiest core decides, up at once, down after a delay, step-wise thermal limit) is the common design of that
  file, UniXNU-sheng's below and Linux's schedutil/step_wise; PianoThermal's thresholds, caps and code are its own.
  Every one of these facts is also checked against piano's own DT (docs/drivers/thermal.md section 2).

UniXNU-sheng (unixnu-research/UniXNU-sheng, main 00ba90984e831e4c6ce30ec3d8a56e6434e9f1af, unixnu.lock pin."UniXNU-sheng"),
BSD-2-Clause-Patent, package/CpuFreqProbe.cpp (sha256 f442c044d6cf403ce8ff164a58ac3c67dcb7a1a82af50ce7e9bc1db95c11fd8a):
  Design only (SM8550's EPSS cpufreq-hw registers are not piano's and are not used): a default-off level ladder (report, fixed,
  governor), the busy share of the busiest CPU from its idle time, schedutil's 1.25 margin, a hispeed jump, up at once / down only
  after several windows that asked for less.

Specifications read, never copied:
  - Arm System Control and Management Interface (SCMI), DEN0056: the shared-memory transport, the message header, the performance
    domain management protocol (Scmi.h);
  - Linux (GPL-2.0, as the specification only): drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens-v2.c and tsens.c (register offsets and fields),
    drivers/mailbox/qcom-cpucp-mbox.c (the doorbell offset), drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c and shmem.c (cross-check of the
    layouts), drivers/thermal/gov_step_wise.c (the shape of the thermal limit);
  - XNU (APSL-2.0, the k27 tree): processor_info's PROCESSOR_CPU_LOAD_INFO, thread_bind, reboot_kernel, IOPMrootDomain (why the
    thermal emergency sleep and the root domain's thermal warning are not used: docs/drivers/thermal.md section 5).

B6, the board thermistors on the PMIC ADC (Ntc.h, AdcChannels.h, PmicAdc.h, BoardTemps.h, PianoThermalAdc.cpp,
tests/adc_host.cpp, package/include/PianoBoardTemps.h, tooling/k27/check-adc-map.py, tooling/k27/check-ntc-curve.py; 2026-11-11):
new code, no source file copied. Specifications only (no code, comment or table copied; GPL-2.0): the Ubuntu piano kernel
(unixnu-research/ubuntu-ref/kernel, branch piano/dev, 7f8d6bedde479a01f4a05d6d0581b43c7fd20a01):
  - drivers/iio/adc/qcom-spmi-adc5-gen3.c (sha256 05eed2b8ff996ecc1f454fcf55f6fc2cef2a28af2fca6fac3b5b35ea96fc81bf) and
    include/linux/iio/adc/qcom-adc5-gen3-common.h (sha256 1589c9d7fa861c7c04966cab55ee64a3d42a77c755f39d57b95fea1704bc09f4): the SDAM
    byte layout, the immediate conversion on SDAM 0 channel 0, the handshake wait (150 x 100 us), the 501 ms conversion bound, the
    status clear, the decimation and settle encodings, Gen4's SID/bus layout and its 0x8000-is-valid rule (Ubuntu's K:5812ec75bb03);
  - drivers/iio/adc/qcom-vadc-common.c (sha256 a196dd0eb63dfee153284b60c4ea56ab4cf8ef64755f93b76b5149f6b53d4613): code -> resistance
    (R = Rpu * code / (full scale - code), full scale 2^14 for Gen3, 0xffff for Gen4), the 100 kOhm pull-up, the part's name
    (NTCG104EF104). Its adcmap7_100k table is not copied or stored: tooling/k27/check-ntc-curve.py reads it from a Linux tree at run
    time to compare (docs/drivers/thermal.md 12.3: its temperatures are degrees C * 1024);
  - drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c (sha256 320e71b64915eb4e32be90b49fd65f12da2241e877bf4f68f0c0c1eb4ab3e28d): the v7 channel offsets,
    command word, status bits, write data registers, the owner table, the 1000 x 1 us transaction wait, EE 0's choice among APIDs;
  - drivers/nvmem/qcom-spmi-sdam.c (sha256 a684073c3d139e6a22fc5be1e1530f1c774dc6d2546a30594ec50c9a1f75eebb): SDAM memory from
    0x40, the size register 0x44, the PBS trigger 0xe5;
  - drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-spmi-gpio.c (sha256 546efbe1601c05b7739b8c1fecd317b228a348699637a85aa59951eedaf87f51): PMIC GPIO
    TYPE 0x10, MODE_CTL 0x40, EN_CTL 0x46 bit 7 (high-impedance when clear);
  - arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts (sha256 79fe7c8009621e4fe00423a10218eacee6b92294ee978a5044026d0e05d127dd): the
    thermistor pins, and that charger1_therm is on PMIH0108 GPIO 12, another EE's pin left high-impedance by the firmware.
  The channel map itself is the piano boot DT's (out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb, sha256
  50636effb5f54306ec0ab9a3061cd163d7f003d8797e04585a33205918856840), checked by tooling/k27/check-adc-map.py at every build.
  The thermistor curve is computed from the part's published parameters (R25 100 kOhm, B25/50 4250 K, B25/85 4311 K, the TDK
  NTCG / Murata NCP 100 kOhm class) by a Steinhart-Hart fit (Ntc.h; tests/adc_host.cpp repeats the derivation); the SPMI facts are
  also those of package/PianoPower/SpmiObserver.h and k27 0057 (this repository).
